/home/sat/mcrl-v025-pilot-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:85:The C2 tie-break diagnostic is the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose C2 head score is exactly equal to the incumbent's under the FULL arm, i.e. C2 cannot discriminate the move and the ranking falls through to C1 plus the stable configuration-ID tie-break. `c2_tie_frequency` is the fraction of anchor-seed decisions with any such tie; `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` is the mean per-decision tie fraction. See DEFECTS.
